  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Transportation obligated $9.4B in FY2026 to date on federal contracts. The agency executed 11,417 awards, with an average award size of $826K, and obligations were up 4.5% year over year. Recent fiscal years show a steady increase from $7B in FY21 to $9.4B in FY26, with intermediate totals of $8B in FY22, $8.7B in FY23, $8.6B in FY24, and $9B in FY25. Engineering Services is the single largest NAICS category, receiving $1.4B in obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of Transportation also obligated $1B to Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing and $922M to Telecommunications Resellers. The top vendors by obligations in FY2026 to date include HARRIS CORPORATION at $922M and RAYTHEON COMPANY at $645M. This profile reflects a mix of professional services, telecommunications and manufacturing, transportation construction, and IT and hosting services in the agency’s contract portfolio for the current fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has contract spending changed over recent years?",
        "body": "The Department of Transportation obligated $9.4B in FY26 to date, up 4.5% year over year. Obligations rose from $7B in FY21 to $9.4B in FY26 with FY22 at $8B, FY23 at $8.7B, FY24 at $8.6B, and FY25 at $9B. The year-to-date total reflects partial fiscal-year activity and the agency’s multi-year upward trend in obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are the largest buying categories and top suppliers?",
        "body": "Engineering Services received $1.4B in FY2026 to date, making it the largest NAICS category by obligations. Other large categories include Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $1B and Telecommunications Resellers at $922M. HARRIS CORPORATION and RAYTHEON COMPANY lead vendors with $922M and $645M in obligations respectively."
      }
    ]
